{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["He began his reproofs by saying: <b>if you do not hearken to the voice of YHWH your Elohim, to keep and do all His commandments and statutes which I command you today.</b> This without doubt refers to when observance of the Torah's commandments was replaced by different customs and the like, and justice was pushed aside. And so, after he said יוֹלֵךְ ה׳ אוֹתְךָ וְאֶת מַלְכְּךָ (Deuteronomy 28:36) — which is the second part — he returned and said כִּי לֹא שָׁמַעְתָּ בְּקוֹל ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ לִשְׁמֹר מִצְוֹתָיו וְחֻקֹּתָיו אֲשֶׁר צִוָּךְ (Deuteronomy 28:45), meaning: but you did observe what others besides Him commanded or instituted, which is not according to His Torah — as they of blessed memory recounted (Gittin 56a): they did not separate terumah or tithes, so that they required the enactment of Yochanan the High Priest and the decree of demai; they would lock the door against borrowers because of shemittah, so that Hillel was required to enact prozbul; the waters of the sotah, the egla arufa, and the sanhedrin were abolished because of the proliferation of transgressors at the end of the Second Temple period, such that all justice was nullified — as they of blessed memory recounted that men of violence prevailed. This is precisely the situation today in all our exile and lowliness: one who has much wealth, especially one liable to judgment, despises the Torah of the blessed El and the ordinances of His mouth, and exerts himself through Gentiles and their courts to pervert a man in his lawsuit. And so they and their property have sunk to destruction. Through these things the cause of the destruction of the Second Temple is explained, and its persistent ruin through the persistence of its cause."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:29.064968736Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}